  "markdown": "![Finished guest bedroom at Brown's Hotel, Mayfair: pale tree-and-leaf wallcovering behind a green patterned headboard, with velvet and fringed botanical cushions under lit wall lights.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/atelier/browns-bedroom-2000.jpg)\n\nThe art of the finish\n\n# Extraordinary rooms. *Impeccably finished.*\n\nSpecialist wallcovering installation for remarkable hotels, considered homes and ambitious spaces.\n\n[Award-winning (2021): Most Outstanding for Wallcovering Installation, BUILD Magazine 2021 Design & Build Awards](https://web.archive.org/web/20220625070338/https://www.renovart.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/renovart-award.jpeg)\n\n[Explore our work](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/) [Start your project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/)\n\nLONDON & SELECTED UK PROJECTS[ON LOCATION Brown’s Hotel, Mayfair **↗**](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n\n## London wallcovering installers, since 2012.\n\n- [In the trade**Since 2012**](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin)\n- [On the record**31 case studies**](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/)\n- [Recognised**BUILD Magazine, 2021**](https://web.archive.org/web/20220625070338/https://www.renovart.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/renovart-award.jpeg)\n\nHotels and historic commissions\n\n## Rooms we have *finished.*\n\n[View the full hotel record](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/#hotels)\n\n[![Narrow bedside at Brown's Hotel, Mayfair, papered in pale tree-and-leaf wallcovering, with a sculptural bronze lamp, a wall light and a green patterned headboard.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/browns-hotel-mayfair-10-800.webp)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n\nMayfair\n\n### [Brown’s Hotel](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n\n[![Junior Suite at Raffles London at The OWO, Whitehall. Official hotel photograph.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/owo-official-junior-suite-800.webp)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/raffles-london-the-owo/)\n\nWhitehall\n\n### [Raffles London at The OWO](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/raffles-london-the-owo/)\n\nImage: Raffles London at The OWO (official)\n\n[![Finished entrance hall in a private residence at Ten Trinity Square: a wall of dark, banded wallcovering with streaks of silver and gold, framed in pale panelling, behind a round mirror and a tan leather bench.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/fs-residences-01-800.webp)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n\nPrivate Residences, City of London\n\n### [Four Seasons, Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n\n![Dorin Burcus, founder of Mr Wallcover](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/dorin-burcus-portrait-800.webp)\n\nDorin Burcus, founder of Mr Wallcover.\n\nThe people on site\n\n## Dorin Burcus\n\nDorin Burcus founded Mr Wallcover. He has worked in the trade since 2012, starting as a labourer and going on to run wallcovering packages in prime London hotels.\n\nMr Wallcover is a London specialist wallcovering installer founded by Dorin Burcus, in the trade since 2012: survey to aftercare for hotels, homes and makers.\n\nWallcoverings, hung properly.\n\n[Meet Dorin](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin) [How the practice works](https://www.mrwallcover.com/practice/)\n\nHow we work\n\n## Five steps, and the same people throughout.\n\n[Explore the five services](https://www.mrwallcover.com/practice/#service-heading)\n\n1. 01\n\n### Consultation\n\nWe start with a conversation. We advise, and we listen to the date, the building, and the way you need to keep using it.\n\n2. 02\n\n### Scope, room by room\n\nAfter the survey we estimate and write a scope of works by room. Once agreed, that scope is the template for the job. Openings come out of the measure. Pattern repeat and wastage go in.\n\n3. 03\n\n### A leader on the ground\n\nEvery project has a project leader who is your day-to-day contact. They look after the craft, the progress, and what you have been told to expect.\n\n4. 04\n\n### Weekly oversight\n\nOn a longer commission, senior oversight quality-controls the work and agrees with you, each week, what happens next.\n\n5. 05\n\n### The same core team\n\nThe people you meet at the start are the core team that finishes. On a long project, people can stay on site or nearby, where that suits the building and the budget.\n\nAftercare\n\n## The hang is not finished when we leave.\n\nAbout four to six weeks later we come back, once the paper has had a chance to settle. Seams and edges are looked at. For twelve months, workmanship of the hang is guaranteed. Building movement and damp are not.\n\n[Read the aftercare](https://www.mrwallcover.com/aftercare/)\n\nYOUR NEXT ROOM\n\n## Let’s make it *something remarkable.*\n\nHotels, prime residences and specified schemes. Tell us what you have in mind.\n\n[Start your project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder\n",
